<speak>That phrase makes a lot of sense for everyday administration. A system that depends on everyone remembering a complicated rule tends to become fragile. At home, you could keep one folder for items awaiting attention and another for material already filed, with labels that are easy to read. That is just a practical suggestion for organisation, not a request to send us anything. We do not need your household filing to match our internal headings. It should make sense to you first. The bank's correspondence can remain intact, and you can choose a filing arrangement that fits how you naturally look for things.</speak>